            "output": "<path>/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/alpaca-hackathon/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Catalyst Router\n2: \n3: <div align=\"center\">\n4: \n5: **An autonomous, risk-bounded AI agent for Alpaca paper trading**\n6: \n7: `XGBoost signals` · `Dynamic equity universe` · `Long/short equities` · `Immutable decisions`\n8: \n9: </div>\n10: \n11: Catalyst Router turns completed market bars into directional trades, but keeps capital authority\n12: outside the model. A checksummed XGBoost classifier proposes long, short, or abstain; deterministic\n13: code validates market data, sizes risk, claims executable decisions exactly once, and submits\n14: server-protected equity brackets to Alpaca. Sanitized predictions, vetoes, routes, and executions feed a\n15: delayed public flight recorder.\n16: \n17: ## Trading Model\n18: \n19: The order-authorized model is a regularized **XGBoost binary classifier** trained on point-in-time\n20: Alpaca IEX bars for a fixed panel of 12 liquid US equities and ETFs. At runtime it predicts the\n21: probability of a positive four-hour move across a daily dynamic universe, an explicit distribution\n22: shift.\n23: \n24: | Model contract | Implemented behavior |\n25: | --- | --- |\n26: | Candidate | `xgboost_regularized` |\n27: | Artifact | Immutable run `20260828T175917Z`, loaded from S3 and verified by SHA-256 |\n28: | Input | Completed 15-minute regular-session bars, delayed one minute for corrections |\n29: | Horizon | 16 bars / 4 hours |\n30: | Features | Lagged returns, range, VWAP distance, volume ratio, realized volatility, SPY context, relative return, cross-sectional rank, range location, and time of day |\n31: | Runtime universe | Up to 20 liquid, option-enabled symbols ranked from the 100 most active stocks, 50 gainers, and 50 losers; SPY retained as market context |\n32: | Output | Probability mapped to `LONG`, `SHORT`, or `ABSTAIN` |\n33: | Runtime gate | Long at `p >= 0.52`; short at `p <= 0.48`; abstain otherwise |\n34: | Cadence | Poll every 15 seconds; score the latest completed vector per symbol and claim each symbol/bar/model tuple idempotently |\n35: | Portfolio | Rank candidates by confidence, enter at most one per cycle, hold at most six symbols |\n36: \n37: ### From prediction to trade\n38: \n39: ```text\n40: completed IEX bars\n41:         │\n42:         ▼\n43: point-in-time feature vector\n44:         │\n45:         ▼\n46: XGBoost probability ──► LONG / SHORT / ABSTAIN\n47:         │\n48:         ▼\n49: fresh quote + spread + market-hours gates\n50:         │\n51:         ▼\n52: deterministic Risk Governor\n53:         │\n54:         ▼\n55: idempotent Alpaca equity entry\n56:    long/short bracket + broker-hosted exits\n57: ```\n58: \n59: The separation is deliberate: the model chooses direction and confidence, never quantity. The Risk\n60: Governor can reduce or veto every proposal, and the execution gateway alone can construct an Alpaca\n61: order.\n62: \n63: ### Risk envelope\n64: \n65: | Control | Enforced limit |\n66: | --- | ---: |\n67: | Entry notional | 10% of account equity |\n68: | Equity risk per trade | Entry-to-stop loss capped at 1% of equity; reduced to 0.5% after a 2% daily loss |\n69: | Concurrent positions | 6 |\n70: | Total open stop-risk | 5% of equity |\n71: | One correlated exposure group | 5% of equity |\n72: | Freshness and liquidity | Quote at most 5 seconds old; spread at most 15 bps |\n73: | Daily circuit breaker | Halt and flatten at a 4% daily loss |\n74: | Competition circuit breaker | Kill and flatten at a 12% peak-to-current drawdown |\n75: | Session boundary | No entry in the final 15 minutes; flatten inside the final 10 minutes |\n76: \n77: Positions are rejected when the account is blocked, the market is closed, reconciliation is stale,\n78: data quality fails, or the account cannot support both the requested buying power and stop-risk.\n79: Equity entries use server-hosted stop-loss and take-profit brackets. The worker verifies protection on\n80: every poll and risk-halts if a held position loses either protective leg. Directional option execution\n81: is disabled.\n82: \n83: ### P&L and validation evidence\n84: \n85: Alpaca remains the source of truth for paper-account state. The public dashboard reports the equity\n86: curve against cash, net P&L, competition return, daily return, observed drawdown, current risk usage,\n87: and the public decisions that produced those results. Decision and portfolio records are sanitized\n88: and delayed by 15 minutes; current agent status and challenger metadata are sanitized but immediate.\n89: The reporting plane cannot control the agent.\n90: \n91: Historical evidence for the authorized artifact uses four expanding chronological folds, purges\n92: overlapping four-hour labels, and charges 12 bps round trip per selected position.\n93: \n94: | Evidence | Return | Sharpe | Max drawdown | Trades |\n95: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n96: | Mean walk-forward validation | **+1.60%** | **0.61** | See fold results | 394 across 4 folds |\n97: | Diagnostic holdout | **+8.38%** | **3.22** | **3.94%** | 76 |\n98: \n99: Only two of four validation folds were positive, and the holdout was inspected during development.\n100: These results are evidence, not a profitability guarantee; the model received explicit bounded\n101: paper-trading authority despite not meeting its original promotion gate. The full protocol, fold\n102: results, failed experiments, and limitations are documented in\n103: [`docs/training/local-benchmark.md`](docs/training/local-benchmark.md).\n104: \n105: ### Shadow AI research path\n106: \n107: Alongside the live classifier, an AWS Bedrock model converts recent Alpaca News into a typed financial\n108: Event: direction, magnitude, novelty, surprise, confidence, horizon, affected symbols, and invalidating\n109: evidence. A deterministic router combines that record with price confirmation.\n110: \n111: This path is intentionally `SHADOW_ONLY`. Bedrock cannot size positions, create orders, or affect the\n112: order-authorized model. Malformed, stale, or unbounded output fails closed to `NO_TRADE`. This creates\n113: forward evidence for a future event-aware model without risking competition capital on an unvalidated\n114: LLM strategy.\n115: \n116: ## Alpaca Services\n117: \n118: | Alpaca technology | How Catalyst Router uses it | Authority |\n119: | --- | --- | --- |\n120: | **Paper Trading API** | Reconciles account, clock, positions, and orders; submits equity brackets; closes and flattens exposure | Sole broker and P&L authority |\n121: | **Market Data API** | Fetches IEX bars and quotes plus market screeners | Read-only market evidence |\n122: | **News API** | Reads the latest symbol-scoped articles for Bedrock Event extraction | Shadow evidence only |\n123: | **`alpaca-py` SDK** | Typed runtime adapter for trading, account state, historical bars, quotes, and news | Private worker only |\n124: | **Alpaca CLI** | Paper-account diagnostics and judge-friendly dry-run demonstrations through `scripts/alpaca-paper` | Read-only; submit is allowed only with `--dry-run` |\n125: | **Alpaca MCP server** | Not connected in this version; the runtime does not expose an LLM-controlled broker tool path | No trading authority |\n126: \n127: The broker adapter is hard-pinned to `https://paper-api.alpaca.markets`. The CLI wrapper rejects\n128: `--live`, rejects mutating commands, and keeps production execution inside the tested Python gateway.\n129: \n130: ## Usage\n131: \n132: ### Prerequisites\n133: \n134: - Python 3.14+\n135: - [`uv`](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)\n136: - Alpaca paper-trading credentials\n137: - Node.js and npm only when running the dashboard\n138: - Docker only for the DynamoDB integration test\n139: \n140: ### Install and verify\n141: \n142: ```bash\n143: uv sync --group inference\n144: uv run pytest\n145: ```\n146: \n147: Provide paper credentials through `.env` or the process environment:\n148: \n149: ```dotenv\n150: ALPACA_KEY=your-paper-key\n151: ALPACA_SECRET=your-paper-secret\n152: ```\n153: \n154: Confirm that the credentials resolve to a paper account and inspect sanitized state:\n155: \n156: ```bash\n157: uv run catalyst-router check-alpaca\n158: uv run catalyst-router reconcile\n159: ```\n160: \n161: ### Run the reporting experience\n162: \n163: Start the read-only API:\n164: \n165: ```bash\n166: uv run catalyst-router serve\n167: ```\n168: \n169: In another terminal, start the dashboard:\n170: \n171: ```bash\n172: npm --prefix dashboard ci\n173: npm --prefix dashboard run dev\n174: ```\n175: \n176: Open `http://localhost:3000`. Development uses the deployed CloudFront API configured in\n177: `dashboard/.env.development` by default. To point it at the local API instead, start it with:\n178: \n179: ```bash\n180: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000 npm --prefix dashboard run dev\n181: ```\n182: \n183: API documentation is available at\n184: `http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs`; useful probes include:\n185: \n186: ```bash\n187: curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/health\n188: curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/ready\n189: curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/public/status\n190: ```\n191: \n192: `/ready` returns `503` until the current state-store epoch has been reconciled.\n193: \n194: ### Run the autonomous paper worker\n195: \n196: Paper execution is disabled by default. A trading worker needs the authorized artifact in S3, shared\n197: DynamoDB state, and explicit execution authority:\n198: \n199: ```dotenv\n200: AWS_REGION=us-east-1\n201: STATE_BACKEND=dynamodb\n202: DYNAMODB_TABLE=catalyst-router-local\n203: COMPETITION_ID=alpaca-hackathon-2026\n204: RUNTIME_ROLE=worker\n205: \n206: CHALLENGER_MANIFEST_URI=s3://your-bucket/models/20260828T175917Z/manifest.json\n207: REDACTED\n208: PAPER_EXECUTION_ENABLED=true\n209: MODEL_EXECUTION_ENABLED=true\n210: MODEL_OPTIONS_EXECUTION_ENABLED=false\n211: MODEL_AUTHORITY=PAPER_LIVE\n212: MODEL_DECISION_GATE=0.52\n213: ```\n214: \n215: To also enable the shadow news path, configure `LLM_EVENTS_ENABLED=true`, `BEDROCK_MODEL_ID`, and\n216: `BEDROCK_PROMPT_VERSION=event-v1`. It still has no order authority.\n217: \n218: The default in-memory backend is process-local, so separate API, control, and worker processes do not\n219: share it. Reconcile the DynamoDB store, grant authority, then start the worker:\n220: \n221: ```bash\n222: uv run catalyst-router reconcile\n223: uv run catalyst-router resume --reason \"paper competition start\"\n224: uv run catalyst-router worker\n225: ```\n226: \n227: `resume` refuses whenever Alpaca has an existing position or open order. Operator controls are\n228: authenticated through local/AWS execution identity and are never exposed by the public API:\n229: \n230: ```bash\n231: uv run catalyst-router pause --reason \"operator review\"\n232: uv run catalyst-router flatten --reason \"close all paper exposure\"\n233: uv run catalyst-router kill --reason \"disable autonomous execution\"\n234: ```\n235: \n236: ### Inspect with the Alpaca CLI\n237: \n238: ```bash\n239: brew install alpacahq/tap/cli\n240: scripts/alpaca-paper doctor\n241: scripts/alpaca-paper account get --jq '{status, trading_blocked, options_trading_level}'\n242: scripts/alpaca-paper order submit --symbol AAPL --side buy --qty 1 --type market --dry-run\n243: ```\n244: \n245: ### Train a challenger\n246: \n247: ```bash\n248: make train-local\n249: ```\n250: \n251: The current runner compares deterministic baselines, linear models, histogram boosting, and XGBoost\n252: on five-minute bars with a 48-bar/four-hour horizon using purged chronological walk-forward\n253: validation. It stores cached bars, checksummed Parquet datasets, manifests, and models under ignored\n254: `.local/training/` paths. These `bar-features-v3` artifacts remain `SHADOW_ONLY`; this command does not\n255: reproduce or replace the authorized 15-minute `bar-features-v2` artifact. See\n256: [`docs/training/five-minute-pipeline.md`](docs/training/five-minute-pipeline.md).\n257: \n258: Run the complete quality gate with `make check`.\n259: \n260: ## Architecture\n261: \n262: ```mermaid\n263: flowchart LR\n264:     subgraph Alpaca\n265:         Bars[IEX bars + quotes]\n266:         News[News API]\n267:         Paper[Paper Trading API]\n268:     end\n269: \n270:     subgraph Private[Private execution plane]\n271:         Worker[ECS Fargate worker]\n272:         Model[XGBoost model]\n273:         Event[Bedrock Event extractor]\n274:         Risk[Risk Governor]\n275:         Gateway[Idempotent execution gateway]\n276:     end\n277: \n278:     subgraph State[Durable state]\n279:         S3[S3 model artifacts]\n280:         DDB[(DynamoDB decisions + orders)]\n281:         Secrets[Secrets Manager]\n282:     end\n283: \n284:     subgraph Public[Read-only reporting plane]\n285:         API[App Runner API]\n286:         CDN[CloudFront]\n287:         UI[Static dashboard]\n288:     end\n289: \n290:     Bars --> Worker\n291:     News --> Event\n292:     Event -. shadow records .-> DDB\n293:     S3 --> Model --> Worker\n294:     Secrets --> Worker\n295:     Worker --> Risk --> Gateway --> Paper\n296:     Paper -->|reconciliation| Worker\n297:     Worker --> DDB\n298:     DDB --> API --> CDN --> UI\n299: ```\n300: \n301: ### Execution lifecycle\n302: \n303: 1. **Reconcile.** Alpaca is authoritative for account, position, and order state. Startup creates a\n304:    fenced execution epoch before any new exposure is allowed.\n305: 2. **Observe.** The worker polls Alpaca every 15 seconds, accepts bars one minute after completion, and\n306:    builds the latest point-in-time vector for each runtime-universe symbol.\n307: 3. **Predict once.** A deterministic decision ID claims each latest symbol/bar/model tuple in DynamoDB\n308:    so retries and restarts cannot execute it twice. Intermediate bars missed during downtime are not\n309:    backfilled.\n310: 4. **Govern.** Fresh quotes, spread, market hours, buying power, stop-risk, group exposure, daily loss,\n311:    and competition drawdown are evaluated outside model authority.\n312: 5. **Execute safely.** A UUID5 client order ID and SHA-256 request hash claim one Alpaca equity bracket.\n313:    Ambiguous submissions are queried by client ID before the gateway changes local state.\n314: 6. **Report.** Immutable records feed a separate read-only API and delayed public dashboard. Public\n315:    infrastructure has no Alpaca credentials or write permission to operational state.\n316: \n317: ### Repository map\n318: \n319: | Path | Responsibility |\n320: | --- | --- |\n321: | `src/catalyst_router/challenger.py` | Artifact verification and XGBoost inference |\n322: | `src/catalyst_router/training.py` | Feature construction, labels, walk-forward training |\n323: | `src/catalyst_router/risk.py` | Deterministic sizing, limits, and vetoes |\n324: | `src/catalyst_router/execution.py` | Signal ranking, order planning, idempotency, circuit breakers |\n325: | `src/catalyst_router/adapters/` | Alpaca, Bedrock, DynamoDB, and in-memory adapters |\n326: | `src/catalyst_router/reporting.py` | Sanitized public portfolio projections |\n327: | `dashboard/` | Statically exported Next.js public flight recorder |\n328: | `infra/environments/prod/` | OpenTofu for ECS, App Runner, DynamoDB, S3, CloudFront, IAM, and observability |\n329: \n330: The central design rule is simple: **AI proposes; deterministic code disposes; Alpaca reconciles.**\n\n(End of file - total 330 lines)\n</content>",
