          "type": "text",
          "text": "## Objective\n- Maintain and refine the 7-slide Reveal.js pitch deck in `presentation.html` for Catalyst Router.\n- Current request: make the text for each results benchmark/metric slightly smaller.\n\n## Important Details\n- Design: Alpaca-inspired `#FCD72B` yellow, black typography, warm off-white, square cards, sparse layouts.\n- Hosted fonts:\n  - `https://files.alpaca.markets/fonts/BROmega/stylesheet.css`\n  - `https://files.alpaca.markets/fonts/Formular/stylesheet.css`\n- All headings and paragraphs explicitly use `var(--black)`; verified title computed color: `rgb(34, 34, 34)`.\n- Results figures are sourced from the read-only Alpaca paper CLI:\n  - Baseline: `$100,000` on August 26, 2026\n  - Ending equity: `$100,115.01` on September 3, 2026\n  - Net P&L: `+$115.01`\n  - Return: `+0.12%`\n  - Filled orders: `42`\n  - Max drawdown: `-0.19%`\n- Use `Filled Orders`, not `Closed Trades`; query found 42 filled, 31 canceled, 0 rejected orders.\n- XGBoost rationale is a muted `.model-note` below the architecture caption.\n- Repo is paper-trading only; do not use live/mutating Alpaca commands.\n- `README.md` was pre-existing modified; do not alter it.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Created and restyled `presentation.html` using Reveal.js `@5.1.0` and Mermaid `@11`.\n- Implemented 7 slides: title, thesis, architecture, Alpaca services, guardrails, results, closing.\n- Fixed Mermaid rendering to avoid hidden Reveal-slide sizing issues.\n- Updated favicon to yellow background with black mark.\n- Added black color override for `.reveal h1, .reveal h2, .reveal h3, .reveal p`.\n- Added architecture XGBoost rationale:\n  - `Why XGBoost: it is a compact, reproducible fit for point-in-time tabular market features, with probability outputs that map cleanly to deterministic long, short, or abstain gates.`\n- Retrieved paper-account performance with:\n  - `scripts/alpaca-paper account get`\n  - `scripts/alpaca-paper account portfolio --period 1M --timeframe 1D`\n  - `scripts/alpaca-paper account activity list --activity-types FILL`\n  - `scripts/alpaca-paper order list --status closed`\n- Replaced Results placeholders with sourced statistics and provenance line.\n- Browser checks of cover, architecture, and Results slides succeeded with zero console errors.\n- `git diff --check` passed after changes; temporary local servers were stopped.\n\n### Active\n- Reduce the Results slide benchmark/metric text slightly; likely adjust `.number` (currently `font-size: 1.45em`) and/or `.metric-label` (currently `font-size: 0.34em`) in `presentation.html`.\n- Verify the change visually against the attached screenshot and ensure no overflow.\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Inspect the Results metric CSS and slightly reduce the relevant metric number/label font size in `presentation.html`.\n2. Serve `presentation.html`, verify slide `#/5` at presentation scale and browser console, then run `git diff --check`.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `presentation.html`: entire Reveal.js deck; CSS includes `.metrics`, `.number`, `.metric-label`, `.model-note`, Results slide, and Mermaid architecture.\n- `README.md`: pre-existing modification; do not alter.\n- `CONTEXT.md`: Catalyst Router domain definitions and paper-trading context.\n- `docs/agents/domain.md`: required domain-documentation reading guidance.\n- `docs/adr/0011-separate-alpaca-runtime-and-agent-tool-authority.md`: Alpaca SDK/MCP/CLI roles; CLI is for operator inspection/demo.\n- `docs/adr/0013-authorize-the-model-for-paper-execution.md`: XGBoost paper-execution authority and deterministic safeguards.\n- `scripts/alpaca-paper`: read-only safety wrapper around Alpaca CLI; rejects live and mutating operations.\n- `src/catalyst_router/cli.py`: `catalyst-router check-alpaca` implementation.\n- `src/catalyst_router/adapters/alpaca.py`: paper-pinned `AlpacaPaperBroker` adapter.",
