            "output": "<path>/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/alpaca-hackathon/docs/adr/0013-authorize-the-model-for-paper-execution.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # ADR-0013: Authorize the Model for Paper Execution\n2: \n3: - Status: Accepted\n4: - Date: 2026-08-28\n5: \n6: ## Context\n7: \n8: ADR-0005 kept trained models in shadow mode until they had stable chronological evidence after\n9: costs. The selected regularized XGBoost classifier has positive aggregate validation and diagnostic\n10: holdout results, but only two of four validation folds are positive and the holdout was inspected\n11: during development. It does not meet the original promotion standard.\n12: \n13: The competition operator has explicitly chosen greater paper-trading aggressiveness and accepts the\n14: model risk. The Alpaca account is paper-only, and deterministic risk and execution controls remain\n15: available outside model authority.\n16: \n17: ## Decision\n18: \n19: Authorize the deployed classifier to create long and short equity Trade Intents in Alpaca paper\n20: trading when its directional probability is at least `0.52`. Evaluate only completed 15-minute bars\n21: and begin with the next completed bar after deployment. Poll every 15 seconds to reduce post-close\n22: entry latency without treating repeated polls as new observations.\n23: \n24: Model Trade Intents remain subject to fresh IEX quotes, spread limits, market hours, reconciliation,\n25: deterministic Risk Governor sizing, the concurrent-position bound of ADR-0015, idempotent order\n26: claims, protected bracket exits, drawdown circuit breakers, and end-of-session flattening. The model\n27: cannot choose quantity or bypass a veto.\n28: \n29: ## Consequences\n30: \n31: - Runtime authority is reported as `PAPER_LIVE`, while the artifact retains its recorded shadow\n32:   validation history.\n33: - A prediction at or above `0.52` opens a long; one at or below `0.48` opens a short.\n34: - Lower confidence increases trade frequency and expected false positives.\n35: - Short entries add borrow-availability and rejection risk that historical bar validation did not\n36:   model.\n37: - This decision does not claim that the original promotion evidence was satisfied.\n\n(End of file - total 37 lines)\n</content>",
