esis</h3>\n103:           <h2>Make the model useful,<br />not <span class=\"accent\">all-powerful.</span></h2>\n104:           <p class=\"statement\">AI proposes direction and confidence. Deterministic code owns every dollar of risk.</p>\n105:           <div class=\"three-up\">\n106:             <div class=\"card mint\">\n107:               <div class=\"label\">Observe</div>\n108:               <div class=\"value\">Dynamic universe</div>\n109:               <div class=\"detail\">Liquid equities, IEX prices, and fresh market context.</div>\n110:             </div>\n111:             <div class=\"card blue\">\n112:               <div class=\"label\">Decide</div>\n113:               <div class=\"value\">Long / short / abstain</div>\n114:               <div class=\"detail\">XGBoost scores completed 15-minute bars.</div>\n115:             </div>\n116:             <div class=\"card coral\">\n117:               <div class=\"label\">Govern</div>\n118:               <div class=\"value\">Risk first</div>\n119:               <div class=\"detail\">The model cannot size, submit, or bypass a veto.</div>\n120:             </div>\n121:           </div>\n122:         </section>\n123: \n124:         <section>\n125:           <h3>Model Architecture</h3>\n126:           <h2>One narrow path to an order.</h2>\n127:           <div class=\"architecture\">\n128:             <pre class=\"mermaid\">\n129: flowchart LR\n130:   subgraph A[Alpaca]\n131:     MD[IEX bars + quotes]\n132:     N[News]\n133:     PT[Paper Trading]\n134:   end\n135:   subgraph C[Catalyst Router]\n136:     U[Dynamic universe]\n137:     M[XGBoost classifier]\n138:     R[Risk Governor]\n139:     E[Idempotent execution]\n140:     L[(Decision ledger)]\n141:   end\n142:   MD --> U --> M\n143:   M -->|Long / Short / Abstain| R\n144:   R -->|Approved only| E --> PT\n145:   PT -->|Reconcile| E\n146:   N -. shadow event evidence .-> L\n147:   M --> L\n148:   R --> L\n149:   E --> L\n150:             </pre>\n151:           </div>\n152:           <p class=\"architecture-note\">The XGBoost model can propose a trade. Only the Risk Governor can approve an Alpaca order.</p>\n153:           <p class=\"model-note\">Why XGBoost: it is a compact, reproducible fit for point-in-time tabular market features, with probability outputs that map cleanly to deterministic long, short, or abstain gates.</p>\n154:         </section>\n155: \n156:         <section>\n157:           <h3>Alpaca, End To End</h3>\n158:           <h2>Alpaca is the market interface<br />and the <span class=\"accent\">source of truth.</span></h2>\n159:           <div class=\"service-grid\">\n160:             <div class=\"card mint\">\n161:               <div class=\"label\">Market Data API</div>\n162:               <div class=\"value\">IEX bars, quotes, screeners</div>\n163:               <div class=\"detail\">Point-in-time model features plus freshness and spread gates.</div>\n164:             </div>\n165:             <div class=\"card blue\">\n166:               <div class=\"label\">News API</div>\n167:               <div class=\"value\">Catalyst evidence</div>\n168:               <div class=\"detail\">Symbol news feeds a shadow-only Bedrock event extractor.</div>\n169:             </div>\n\n(Showing lines 50-169 of 290. Use offset=170 to continue.)\n</content>",
