            "output": "<path>/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/alpaca-hackathon/docs/training/local-benchmark.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Local Challenger Benchmark\n2: \n3: ## Status\n4: \n5: The selected local price-only challenger is `xgboost_regularized` using feature schema\n6: `bar-features-v2` and a four-hour horizon. Its artifact records a `0.60` shadow gate. ADR-0013\n7: authorizes it for Alpaca paper execution with a more aggressive `0.52` runtime gate while preserving\n8: the validation limitations below.\n9: \n10: This benchmark remains historical evidence for the deployed 15-minute artifact. ADR-0014 introduces\n11: the five-minute `bar-features-v3` pipeline in shadow mode; it requires a new benchmark and must not\n12: reuse the results below as promotion evidence.\n13: \n14: ## Five-Minute Shadow Run\n15: \n16: Run `20260829T092122Z` trained on 2,157,716 five-minute bars for 20 symbols from January 2021\n17: through August 29, 2026. After rejecting missing-bar and cross-session feature windows and requiring\n18: same-session four-hour labels, the sample contained 131,294 examples: 107,385 development and\n19: 23,841 diagnostic holdout examples.\n20: \n21: The best runtime-compatible candidate was `xgboost_return_shallow` at an 8 basis-point edge gate.\n22: Its four validation folds produced mean return `-3.57%`, mean Sharpe `-0.36`, mean maximum drawdown\n23: `14.64%`, and selection score `-1.46`; only one fold had positive cumulative return. The diagnostic\n24: holdout returned `-17.21%` with Sharpe `-4.01`, maximum drawdown `17.54%`, and 75 trades.\n25: \n26: The artifact remains `SHADOW_ONLY`, `promotion_eligible=false`, and failed its numeric shadow gate.\n27: It must not replace or inherit authority from the ADR-0013 model.\n28: \n29: ## Protocol\n30: \n31: - Source: raw Alpaca IEX 15-minute regular-session bars.\n32: - Sample: 12 fixed liquid symbols from January 2025 through August 27, 2026.\n33: - Features: lagged returns, range, VWAP distance, volume, volatility, SPY context,\n34:   cross-sectional rank, range location, and time of day. Every feature is available at bar close.\n35: - Validation: four expanding chronological folds with a label-horizon purge.\n36: - Diagnostic holdout: final 15% of timestamps beginning June 1, 2026.\n37: - Simulation: at most three equal-weight long or short positions per non-overlapping rebalance.\n38: - Cost: 12 basis points round trip per selected position.\n39: - Selection score: mean fold Sharpe minus fold-Sharpe dispersion and five times mean drawdown.\n40: \n41: ## Iterations\n42: \n43: | Iteration | Best approach | Horizon | Mean validation return | Diagnostic holdout |\n44: | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n45: | Direction classification, v1 features | Logistic regression | 1 hour | -27.46% | -29.91% |\n46: | Direct return regression, v1 features | Ridge regression | 1 hour | -3.36% | -2.58% |\n47: | Horizon search, v1 features | Robust XGBoost return | 3.25 hours | +0.91% | +12.12% |\n48: | Horizon search, v1 features | Ridge regression | 2 hours | -3.95% | -7.93% |\n49: | Horizon search, v1 features | Robust XGBoost return | 4 hours | +2.78% | +8.78% |\n50: | Contextual v2 features | Regularized XGBoost classifier | 4 hours | +1.60% | +8.38% |\n51: \n52: The final selected configuration was positive in two of four validation folds:\n53: \n54: | Fold | Return | Sharpe | Maximum drawdown | Trades |\n55: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n56: | 1 | -0.13% | 0.04 | 7.33% | 110 |\n57: | 2 | +1.54% | 0.76 | 2.99% | 98 |\n58: | 3 | -1.18% | -0.41 | 8.18% | 90 |\n59: | 4 | +6.19% | 2.05 | 5.96% | 96 |\n60: \n61: Aggregate validation mean Sharpe was `0.61`; the conservative selection score was `-0.62`.\n62: The diagnostic holdout returned `+8.38%`, with Sharpe `3.22`, maximum drawdown `3.94%`,\n63: and 76 trades across 46 invested periods.\n64: \n65: ## Reproduce\n66: \n67: ```bash\n68: make train-local\n69: ```\n70: \n71: Use `--refresh` to replace the cached source bars. The ignored artifact manifest records the data\n72: SHA-256, feature schema, package versions, model parameters, model hash, folds, and ranking.\n73: \n74: ## Limits\n75: \n76: - The holdout was inspected during iterative horizon and feature work, so it is diagnostic rather\n77:   than untouched promotion evidence.\n78: - The fixed universe avoids dynamic selection leakage but does not model historical universe\n79:   construction or delistings.\n80: - Bar data cannot reproduce executable bid/ask prices, halts, borrow availability, or market impact.\n81: - Simulated returns are equal-weight basket returns, not expected account P&L under the Risk Governor.\n82: - The sample has no point-in-time news/event features and cannot compare the full catalyst incumbent.\n83: - Fold instability and 76 diagnostic holdout trades are insufficient for promotion confidence.\n84: \n85: The next valid test is forward collection with quotes, Alpaca News, incumbent decisions, and\n86: realized executable prices. ADR-0013 records the operator's explicit paper-live override; it does not\n87: claim the original promotion criteria were met.\n\n(End of file - total 87 lines)\n</content>",
