iv>\n116:               <div class=\"value\">Long / short / abstain</div>\n117:               <div class=\"detail\">XGBoost scores completed 15-minute bars.</div>\n118:             </div>\n119:             <div class=\"card coral\">\n120:               <div class=\"label\">Govern</div>\n121:               <div class=\"value\">Risk first</div>\n122:               <div class=\"detail\">The model cannot size, submit, or bypass a veto.</div>\n123:             </div>\n124:           </div>\n125:         </section>\n126: \n127:         <section>\n128:           <h3>Model Architecture</h3>\n129:           <h2>One narrow path to an order.</h2>\n130:           <div class=\"architecture\">\n131:             <pre class=\"mermaid\">\n132: flowchart LR\n133:   subgraph A[Alpaca]\n134:     MD[IEX bars + quotes]\n135:     N[News]\n136:     PT[Paper Trading]\n137:   end\n138:   subgraph C[Catalyst Router]\n139:     U[Dynamic universe]\n140:     M[Regularized XGBoost classifier]\n141:     R[Risk Governor]\n142:     E[Idempotent execution]\n143:     L[(Decision ledger)]\n144:   end\n145:   MD --> U --> M\n146:   M -->|Long / Short / Abstain| R\n147:   R -->|Approved only| E --> PT\n148:   PT -->|Reconcile| E\n149:   N -. shadow event evidence .-> L\n150:   M --> L\n151:   R --> L\n152:   E --> L\n153:             </pre>\n154:           </div>\n155:           <p class=\"architecture-note\">The XGBoost model can propose a trade. Only the Risk Governor can approve an Alpaca order.</p>\n156:           <div class=\"model-spec\" aria-label=\"Deployed model specification\">\n157:             <div><strong>350</strong>boosted trees</div>\n158:             <div><strong>4</strong>max depth</div>\n159:             <div><strong>16</strong>point-in-time inputs</div>\n160:             <div><strong>4h</strong>prediction horizon</div>\n161:           </div>\n162:           <p class=\"model-note\">Regularized binary classifier trained on 12 liquid equities and ETFs. Every completed 15-minute bar produ