llout { background: var(--yellow); border: 1.5px solid var(--black); border-radius: 0; margin-top: 0.45em; padding: 0.35em 0.55em; }\n79:       .result-callout p { font-size: 0.58em; margin: 0; }\n80: \n81:       .closing { max-width: 17em; text-align: center; }\n82:       .closing h2 { font-size: 2.12em; }\n83:       .closing p { color: var(--black); }\n84:       .closing .tagline { border-top: 2px solid var(--black); font-size: 0.61em; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 1em; padding-top: 0.7em; }\n85: \n86:       @media (max-width: 700px) {\n87:         .three-up, .metrics, .service-grid { gap: 0.18em; }\n88:         .card { padding: 0.25em 0.3em; }\n89:         .architecture svg { max-height: 330px; }\n90:       }\n91:     </style>\n92:   </head>\n93:   <body>\n94:     <div class=\"reveal\">\n95:       <div class=\"slides\">\n96:         <section class=\"center brand-cover\" data-transition=\"fade\">\n97:           <div>\n98:             <div class=\"eyebrow\">Alpaca Hackathon 2026</div>\n99:             <h1>Catalyst<br /><span class=\"accent\">Router</span></h1>\n100:             <div class=\"title-rule\"></div>\n101:             <p class=\"lede\">An autonomous paper-trading agent where AI finds a signal and deterministic systems protect the capital.</p>\n102:           </div>\n103:           <div class=\"title-footer\">XGBoost signals / Alpaca paper trading / Immutable decisions</div>\n104:         </section>\n105: \n106:         <section>\n107:           <h3>The Thesis</h3>\n108:           <h2>Make the model useful,<br />not <span class=\"accent\">all-powerful.</span></h2>\n109:           <p class=\"statement\">AI proposes direction and confidence. Deterministic code owns every dollar of risk.</p>\n110:           <div class=\"three-up\">\n111:             <div class=\"card mint\">\n112:               <div class=\"label\">Observe</div>\n113:               <div class=\"value\">Dynamic universe</div>\n114:               <div class=\"detail\">Liquid equities, IEX prices, and fresh market context.</div>\n115:             </div>\n116:             <div class=\"card blue\">\n117:               <div class=\"label\">Decide</div>\n118:               <div class=\"value\">Long / short / abstain</div>\n119:               <div class=\"detail\">XGBoost scores completed 15-minute bars.</div>\n120:             </div>\n121:             <div class=\"card coral\">\n122:               <div class=\"label\">Govern</div>\n123:               <div class=\"value\">Risk first</div>\n124:               <div class=\"detail\">The model cannot size, submit, or bypass a veto.</div>\n125:             </div>\n126:           </div>\n127:         </section>\n128: \n129:         <section>\n130:           <h3>Model Architecture</h3>\n131:           <h2>One narrow path to an order.</h2>\n132:           <div class=\"architecture\">\n133:             <pre class=\"mermaid\">\n134: flowchart LR\n135:   subgraph A[Alpaca]\n136:     MD[IEX bars + quotes]\n137:     N[News]\n138:     PT[Paper Trading]\n139:   end\n140:   subgraph C[Catalyst Router]\n141:     U[Dynamic universe]\n142:     M[Regularized XGBoost classifier]\n143:     R[Risk Governor]\n144:     E[Idempotent execution]\n145:     L[(Decision ledger)]\n146:   end\n147:   MD --> U --> M\n148:   M -->|Long / Short / Abstain| R\n149:   R -->|Approved only| E --> PT\n150:   PT -->|Reconcile| E\n151:   N -. shadow event evidence .-> L\n152:   M --> L\n153:   R --> L\n154:   E --> L\n155:             </pre>\n156:           </div>\n157:           <p class=\"architecture-note\">The XGBoost model can propose a trade. Only the Risk Governor can approve an Alpaca order.</p>\n158:           <div class=\"model-spec\" aria-label=\"Deployed model specification\">\n159:             <div class=\"card\"><span>Boosted trees</span><strong>350</strong></div>\n160:             <div class=\"card\"><span>Max depth</span><strong>4</strong></div>\n161:             <div class=\"card\"><span>Point-in-time inputs</span><strong>16</strong></div>\n162:             <div class=\"card\"><span>Prediction horizon</span><strong>4h</strong></div>\n163:           </div>\n164:           <p class=\"model-note\">The classifier estimates a positive four-hour move. A probability of 52% or higher indicates enough upside edge for a long position. A probability of 48% or lower indicates the corresponding downside edge for a short position. The 48-52% band abstains from weak signals. This narrow symmetric gate permits more paper trading opportunities while deterministic risk controls retain final authority.</p>\n\n(Showing lines 60-164 of 300. Use offset=165 to continue.)\n</content>",
