        },
        {
          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "**Explaining risk halt conditions**\n\nI need to explain the situation to the user clearly. There’s a risk halt triggered at a 4% daily loss, and the first option had stale quotes that caused a risk halt flatten. I want to clarify the differences between a risk halt and a kill, emphasizing the importance of preventing further losses during abnormal conditions. It might be best to suggest stopping new entries and starting to flatten once there's a 4% daily loss. Asking if no code is needed could simplify things.",
          "time": {
            "start": 1788515391190,
            "end": 1788515393155
          },
          "metadata": {
            "openai": {
              "itemId": "rs_06b0c56290b88422016a9a943f27a887d2a125b0b54dea9526",
              "reasoningEncryptedContent": "REDACTED"
            }
          },
          "id": "prt_06bd316d6001T4MH2A0Wf1SdXS",
          "sessionID": "ses_f9456c2f9ffeQBfnqIET588Jmg",
          "messageID": "msg_06bd30ed3001CHjYoeDbyVmvsF"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A risk halt stops the system from opening new exposure when conditions show that losses or operational data quality are outside the intended risk envelope.\n\nIts motivation is containment:\n\n- Prevents a sequence of bad trades from compounding into a larger drawdown.\n- Forces the system to flatten or manage down existing exposure instead of continuing normally.\n- Protects against operational failures such as stale quotes, failed reconciliation, or broken exit supervision.\n- Preserves capital until an operator can investigate and resume safely.\n\nIn this case, an option quote stayed stale beyond the supervision window. The halt prevented the system from relying on unreliable prices while holding leveraged option positions.",
          "time": {
            "start": 1788515393157,
            "end": 1788515394518
          },
          "metadata": {
            "openai": {
              "itemId": "msg_06b0c56290b88422016a9a9441092487d2ba85edf7328549bc",
