          "text": "## Objective\n- Add a factual Results-slide note about the prior day’s +$309.97 equity peak and the subsequent option-integration loss.\n- Continue refining `presentation.html` while preserving the deck’s visual and wording preferences.\n\n## Important Details\n- Deck style uses Alpaca yellow `#FCD72B`, black typography, warm off-white, square bordered cards, and sparse layouts.\n- User wording preference for the new explanatory text: no ADR reference, no semicolons, no em dashes, and no colons.\n- Alpaca paper account is read-only. Do not use live or mutating commands.\n- Current account equity is `$100,115.01`, equal to `+$115.01` from the `$100,000` baseline.\n- Prior-day account equity was `$100,309.97`, or `+$309.97`.\n- One-day change from the prior-day peak to current equity was `-$194.96`.\n- `docs/adr/0018-return-directional-execution-to-equities.md` attributes approximately `$194` in option losses to the first paper-live option session, including an earlier GDX trade.\n- User described the option integration as producing very bad performance. Phrase this as a factual result rather than an unsupported causal claim.\n- Current model facts shown in the deck:\n  - 350 boosted trees\n  - Maximum depth 4\n  - 16 point-in-time inputs\n  - Four-hour prediction horizon\n- Mermaid labels use `28px` source font size. Final compact horizontal diagram renders labels at approximately `20px` on-slide.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Reduced Results metric value font size from `1.45em` to `1.25em`.\n- Reordered Results metric labels above values.\n- Added model specification cards to the architecture slide with descriptors above values.\n- Added spacing between model cards and explanation text.\n- Added and refined threshold explanation without ADR reference, colons, semicolons, or em dashes.\n- Reworked Mermaid architecture into a compact horizontal flow:\n  - `IEX market data` → `Universe` → `XGBoost` → `Risk Governor` → `Execution` → `Paper trading`\n  - `News` shadow events and decisions feed `Ledger`\n- Verified Mermaid slide rendering without console errors and with all architecture content visible.\n- `git diff --check` passed after prior presentation edits.\n- Verified Alpaca paper-account figures with:\n  - `scripts/alpaca-paper account get`\n  - `scripts/alpaca-paper account portfolio --period 1M --timeframe 1D`\n  - `scripts/alpaca-paper order list --status closed`\n- Confirmed the September 2 equity peak of `$100,309.97` and September 3 equity of `$100,115.01`.\n- Confirmed option trades were present in closed orders and the accepted option-execution review records approximately `$194` of loss.\n\n### Active\n- Add a note or callout to the Results slide in `presentation.html` stating the prior-day `+$309.97` peak and `-$194.96` decline after option execution was introduced.\n- Ensure the new note follows the user’s punctuation constraints and fits the slide.\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Inspect the remainder of the Results slide and add a concise factual performance note beneath the metrics or provenance.\n2. Serve `presentation.html`, verify slide `#/5` at presentation scale with no overflow or console errors, then run `git diff --check`.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `presentation.html`: Reveal.js deck, architecture Mermaid diagram, model cards, and Results slide to update.\n- `docs/adr/0018-return-directional-execution-to-equities.md`: records option-session freshness failure, risk halt, flattening, and approximately `$194` loss.\n- `scripts/alpaca-paper`: read-only Alpaca CLI safety wrapper.\n- `README.md`: pre-existing modification, do not alter.\n- `CONTEXT.md`: Catalyst Router domain definitions and paper-trading context.\n- `docs/agents/domain.md`: domain-documentation guidance.\n- `docs/adr/0013-authorize-the-model-for-paper-execution.md`: model gates and deterministic safeguards.\n- `src/catalyst_router/training.py`: feature schema and 16 feature names.\n- `scripts/train-challeng