        {
          "type": "tool",
          "tool": "bash",
          "callID": "call_EyIn9SyK0HZbQaefAKyQObqT",
          "state": {
            "status": "completed",
            "input": {
              "command": "pdftotext \"Catalyst-Router-Alpaca-Hackathon.pdf\" -",
              "workdir": "/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/alpaca-hackathon"
            },
            "output": "ALPACA HACKATHON 2026\n\nCatalyst\nRouter\nAn autonomous paper-trading agent\nwhere AI finds a signal and deterministic\nsystems protect the capital.\n\n1\n\n\fTHE THESIS\n\nMake the model useful,\nnot all-powerful.\nAI proposes direction and confidence.\nDeterministic code owns every dollar of\nrisk.\nOBSERVE\n\nDECIDE\n\nGOVERN\n\nDynamic universe\n\nLong / short / abstain\n\nRisk first\n\nLiquid equities, IEX prices, and fresh market\ncontext.\n\nXGBoost scores completed 15-minute bars.\n\nThe model cannot size, submit, or bypass a\nveto.\n\n2\n\n\fMODEL ARCHITECTURE\n\nOne narrow path to an order.\nThe XGBoost model can propose a trade. Only the Risk Governor can approve an Alpaca order.\nBOOSTED TREES\n\nMAX DEPTH\n\nPOINT-IN-TIME INPUTS\n\nPREDICTION HORIZON\n\n350\n\n4\n\n16\n\n4H\n\nThe classifier estimates a positive four-hour move. A probability of 52% or higher indicates enough upside edge for a long\nposition. A probability of 48% or lower indicates the corresponding downside edge for a short position. The 48-52% band abstains\nfrom weak signals. This narrow symmetric gate permits more paper trading opportunities while deterministic risk controls retain\nfinal authority.\n\n3\n\n\fA L PA C A , E N D TO E N D\n\nAlpaca is the market interface\nand the source of truth.\nMARKET DATA API\n\nNEWS API\n\nIEX bars, quotes, screeners\n\nCatalyst evidence\n\nPoint-in-time model features plus freshness and spread gates.\n\nSymbol news feeds a shadow-only Bedrock event extractor.\n\nPAPER TRADING API\n\nALPACA-PY + CLI\n\nBrackets and reconciliation\n\nTyped runtime and safe demo\n\nBroker-hosted exits; account, order, and P&L authority.\n\nPython worker executes; CLI supports read-only diagnostics and dry runs.\n\n4\n\n\fB U I LT TO S U R V I V E\n\nEvery trade must earn\npermission to exist.\nMARKET GATES\n\nPORTFOLIO LIMITS\n\nFAILURE CONTAINMENT\n\nFreshness, spread, hours\n\n1% risk per trade\n\nBrackets + circuit breakers\n\nBad or stale data resolves to no trade.\n\nSix positions max, 5% total stop-risk.\n\nRisk halt at 4% daily loss; kill at 12% drawdown.\n\nAuditable by design: immutable decisions, idempotent order claims, and Alpaca reconciliation after every\nrestart.\n\n5\n\n\fR E S U LTS\n\nPaper-trading performance.\nNET P&L\n\n+$115.01\n\nRETURN\n\n+0.12%\n\nFILLED ORDERS\n\n42\n\nMAX DRAWDOWN\n\n-0.19%\n\nMeasured against Alpaca's $100,000 baseline: the account ended September 3 at $100,115.01.\nPeak before options. The account reached $100,309.97 on September 2, or +$309.97 from baseline. The\nfirst option session on September 3 lost approximately $194 after stale indicative quotes triggered a risk\nhalt and flatten. Option execution is now disabled.\n\n6\n\n\fCATALYST ROUTER\n\nIntelligence with\nboundaries.\nWe are not asking an LLM to trade. We are\nbuilding a verifiable system that uses models\nwhere they help and controls where they matter.\nAI proposes. Deterministic code disposes. Alpaca\nreconciles.\n\n7\n\n\f",
            "metadata": {
              "output": "ALPACA HACKATHON 2026\n\nCatalyst\nRouter\nAn autonomous paper-trading agent\nwhere AI finds a signal and deterministic\nsystems protect the capital.\n\n1\n\n\fTHE THESIS\n\nMake the model useful,\nnot all-powerful.\nAI proposes direction and confidence.\nDeterministic code owns every dollar of\nrisk.\nOBSERVE\n\nDECIDE\n\nGOVERN\n\nDynamic universe\n\nLong / short / abstain\n\nRisk first\n\nLiquid equities, IEX prices, and fresh market\ncontext.\n\nXGBoost scores completed 15-minute bars.\n\nThe model cannot size, submit, or bypass a\nveto.\n\n2\n\n\fMODEL ARCHITECTURE\n\nOne narrow path to an order.\nThe XGBoost model can propose a trade. Only the Risk Governor can approve an Alpaca order.\nBOOSTED TREES\n\nMAX DEPTH\n\nPOINT-IN-TIME INPUTS\n\nPREDICTION HORIZON\n\n350\n\n4\n\n16\n\n4H\n\nThe classifier estimates a positive four-hour move. A probability of 52% or higher indicates enough upside edge for a long\nposition. A probability of 48% or lower indicates the corresponding downside edge for a short position. The 48-52% band abstains\nfrom weak signals. This narrow symmetric gate permits more paper trading opportunities while deterministic risk controls retain\nfinal authority.\n\n3\n\n\fA L PA C A , E N D TO E N D\n\nAlpaca is the market interface\nand the source of truth.\nMARKET DATA API\n\nNEWS API\n\nIEX bars, quotes, screeners\n\nCatalyst evidence\n\nPoint-in-time model features plus freshness and spread gates.\n\nSymbol news feeds a shadow-only Bedrock event extractor.\n\nPAPER TRADING API\n\nALPACA-PY + CLI\n\nBrackets and reconciliation\n\nTyped runtime and safe demo\n\nBroker-hosted exits; account, order, and P&L authority.\n\nPython worker executes; CLI supports read-only diagnostics and dry runs.\n\n4\n\n\fB U I LT TO S U R V I V E\n\nEvery trade must earn\npermission to exist.\nMARKET GATES\n\nPORTFOLIO LIMITS\n\nFAILURE CONTAINMENT\n\nFreshness, spread, hours\n\n1% risk per trade\n\nBrackets + circuit breakers\n\nBad or stale data resolves to no trade.\n\nSix positions max, 5% total stop-risk.\n\nRisk halt at 4% daily loss; kill at 12% drawdown.\n\nAuditable by design: immutable decisions, idempotent order claims, and Alpaca reconciliation after every\nrestart.\n\n5\n\n\fR E S U LTS\n\nPaper-trading performance.\nNET P&L\n\n+$115.01\n\nRETURN\n\n+0.12%\n\nFILLED ORDERS\n\n42\n\nMAX DRAWDOWN\n\n-0.19%\n\nMeasured against Alpaca's $100,000 baseline: the account ended September 3 at $100,115.01.\nPeak before options. The account reached $100,309.97 on September 2, or +$309.97 from baseline. The\nfirst option session on September 3 lost approximately $194 after stale indicative quotes triggered a risk\nhalt and flatten. Option execution is now disabled.\n\n6\n\n\fCATALYST ROUTER\n\nIntelligence with\nboundaries.\nWe are not asking an LLM to trade. We are\nbuilding a verifiable system that uses models\nwhere they help and controls where they matter.\nAI proposes. Deterministic code disposes. Alpaca\nreconciles.\n\n7\n\n\f",
